# g75-fu-engine-live (desktop): what the lead applies after the wave. Apply after PROTO-WIRE has taken pending-rows/g75-fu-engine-live.rows
# (the generated types of the three requests and the two PageDescriptor fields are what the handlers in host/browser-engine/signin.ts and
# pages.ts are typed against).
#
# 1. host/connection.ts, HOST_CAPABILITIES: declare the capability, beside `windows: true` (no switch; the one line DESKTOP-WIRE-G7 held back
#    in deferred-g7.md "NOT applied: s4-wire-desktop.wire item 1"). With it the core routes every Browser Use action of this PC to the
#    engine, which now carries what the engine lacked (network requestId, fill savedAccount, the sign-in hooks, the turn end, the blank-page
#    discards: results/g8/impl-g75-fu-engine-live.json):
#
#      // `host/browser/*` engine methods (host/browser-engine/index.ts). A core that does not compose the engine ignores it.
#      browserEngine: { version: 1, features: ['inputBatch', 'snapshot', 'lease', 'blob'] },
#
# 2. browser/host-agent.ts and browser/host.ts: createBrowserHostAgent returns the sign-in port the engine lane is built with, and
#    BrowserEnginePorts.signIn (host/browser-engine/index.ts, done) takes it. Checked: with this diff applied, tsc -p tsconfig.node.json and
#    -p tsconfig.web.json report nothing. The diff below the marker line is the text itself, as a unified diff of the files in the tree
#    now: copy everything after the marker into a file and `git apply` it from the repository root.
#
# 3. Nothing else: serveBrowserEngine already engages the lane from the first engine method the core calls.
#
----- patch (everything below this line) -----
diff --git a/apps/desktop/src/main/browser/host-agent.ts b/apps/desktop/src/main/browser/host-agent.ts
index 0a30fd2a05..ac53f0db7d 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/src/main/browser/host-agent.ts
